(4527786, 647949, 58430, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tootsweet:</b></div><hr/><i> Animal shots are so difficult to get right.  This one is about 80% right.  The eyes are too washed out for the picture to have that "Wow" factor. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You may need to calibrate your monitor.  The eyes are not washed out on my desktop or on my personal laptop...but they are washed out on my work laptop because the monitor is not calibrated.</td>', 'Originally posted by tootsweet: Animal shots are so difficult to get right.  This one is about 80% right.  The eyes are too washed out for the picture to have that "Wow" factor.   You may need to calibrate your monitor.  The eyes are not washed out on my desktop or on my personal laptop...but they are washed out on my work laptop because the monitor is not calibrated.', '2008-02-29 10:59:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4527787, 647949, 58430, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> good focus, crop is a bit unlucky. you managed to catch the cats emotions, but overall this has less impact compared to the original </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Unfortunately this is the original.  I did not crop this image.  The cat was being very difficult and would not look at me.</td>', 'Originally posted by eyewave: good focus, crop is a bit unlucky. you managed to catch the cats emotions, but overall this has less impact compared to the original   Unfortunately this is the original.  I did not crop this image.  The cat was being very difficult and would not look at me.', '2008-02-29 11:00:18.000000', NULL, 0),
